      "text": "Let \\( f(x) = x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 \\). The solutions to the equation \\( f(x) = 0 \\) are \\( r, s, \\) and \\( t \\). By Vieta's formulas, we know:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 5, \\quad rs + st + tr = 6, \\quad rst = 9.\n\\]\n\nWe aim to compute the value of \\( \\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} \\). We can rewrite this expression using \\( rs + st + tr = 6 \\) and \\( rst = 9 \\):\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{rs \\cdot s + st \\cdot t + tr \\cdot r}{rst} = \\frac{s^2r + t^2s + r^2t}{rst}.\n\\]\nSubstituting \\( rst = 9 \\) into the expression, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{s^2r + t^2s + r^2t}{9}.\n\\]\nWe can use the identity \\( (r+s+t)(rs+st+tr) = r^2s + r^2t + s^2r + s^2t + t^2s + t^2r \\) to find \\( r^2s + s^2r + t^2s + t^2r \\). Expanding the left side, we have:\n\\[\n(r+s+t)(rs+st+tr) = 5(6) = 30.\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\nr^2s + r^2t + s^2r + s^2t + t^2s + t^2r = 30.\n\\]\nSince \\( r^2s + s^2r + t^2s + t^2r = (r^2s + r^2t + s^2r + s^2t) + (t^2s + t^2r) \\), we need to find \\( r^2s + s^2r + t^2s + t^2r \\). Using Vieta's formula \\( rs + st + tr = 6 \\), we can write:\n\\[\nr^2s + s^2r + t^2s + t^2r = (rs + st + tr)(r + s + t) - (rs + st + tr) = 6 \\cdot 5 - 6 = 30 - 6 = 24.\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\nr^2s + s^2r + t^2s + t^2r = 24,\n\\]\nand\n\\[\ns^2r + t^2s + r^2t = r^2s + s^2r + t^2s + t^2r - (rs + st + tr) = 24 - 6 = 18.\n\\]\nTherefore,\n\\[\nr^2s + s^2r + t^2s + t^2r = 18.\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{18}{9} = 2.\n\\]\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}.\n\\]",
