      "text": "Given the polynomial equation \\(x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0\\), we know that \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\) are the roots. By Vieta's formulas, we have:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 5,\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 6,\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 9.\n\\]\n\nWe need to compute the value of \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\). To do this, we will use the fact that \\( \\frac{rs}{t} = \\frac{rs \\cdot st}{rst} = \\frac{r^2 s^2}{rst} = \\frac{r^2 s^2}{9} \\), and similarly for the other terms. So we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{r^2 s^2}{rst} + \\frac{s^2 t^2}{rst} + \\frac{t^2 r^2}{rst} = \\frac{(rs)^2}{rst} + \\frac{(st)^2}{rst} + \\frac{(tr)^2}{rst} = \\frac{(rs)^2 + (st)^2 + (tr)^2}{rst}.\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to compute \\((rs)^2 + (st)^2 + (tr)^2\\). We use the identity:\n\\[\n(rs)^2 + (st)^2 + (tr)^2 = (rs + st + tr)^2 - 2rst(r + s + t).\n\\]\nSubstituting the values from Vieta's formulas, we get:\n\\[\n(rs)^2 + (st)^2 + (tr)^2 = (rs + st + tr)^2 - 2rst(r + s + t) = 6^2 - 2 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 5 = 36 - 90 = -54.\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n\\frac{(rs)^2 + (st)^2 + (tr)^2}{rst} = \\frac{-54}{9} = -6.\n\\]\nTherefore, the value is \\(\\boxed{-6}\\).",
