      "text": "We begin with the given equation:\n\\[\nx^3 - 5x^2 + 6x = 9\n\\]\nFirst, we rearrange it to set it equal to zero:\n\\[\nx^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0\n\\]\nWe know that \\( r, s, \\) and \\( t \\) are the roots of this polynomial. By Vieta's formulas, we know the following relationships among the roots:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 5\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 6\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 9\n\\]\n\nWe need to compute the expression:\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\n\\]\n\nTo simplify this, we first express each fraction in a common form:\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} = \\frac{rs \\cdot s}{t \\cdot s} = \\frac{rsst}{st} = st\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{st}{r} = \\frac{st \\cdot r}{r \\cdot r} = \\frac{strr}{r^2} = tr\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{tr \\cdot s}{s \\cdot s} = \\frac{trss}{s^2} = ts\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = st + tr + ts\n\\]\n\nNotice that this is the same as:\n\\[\n(st + tr + ts)\n\\]\n\nFrom Vieta's formulas, we already know:\n\\[\nst + tr + ts = 6\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
